        "text": "Step 2: Calculate the volume of the spherical tank.\nThe formula for the volume of a sphere is \\(V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\), where \\(r\\) is the radius.\nFor the tank, \\(r = 6\\) cm.\nSo, the volume of the tank is \\(V_{\\text{tank}} = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (6)^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (216) = 288\\pi\\) cubic centimeters."
