  "raw_text": "Step 1: Calculate the volume of the cylindrical beaker.\nThe formula for the volume of a cylinder is \\(V = \\pi r^2 h\\), where \\(r\\) is the radius and \\(h\\) is the height.\nFor the beaker, \\(r = 3\\) cm and \\(h = 8\\) cm.\nSo, the volume of the beaker is \\(V_{\\text{beaker}} = \\pi (3)^2 (8) = 72\\pi\\) cubic centimeters.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the volume of the spherical tank.\nThe formula for the volume of a sphere is \\(V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\), where \\(r\\) is the radius.\nFor the tank, \\(r = 6\\) cm.\nSo, the volume of the tank is \\(V_{\\text{tank}} = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (6)^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (216) = 288\\pi\\) cubic centimeters.\n\nStep 3: Determine how many beakers are needed to fill the tank.\nTo find out how many beakers are needed, divide the volume of the tank by the volume of one beaker.\n\\(\\frac{V_{\\text{tank}}}{V_{\\text{beaker}}} = \\frac{288\\pi}{72\\pi} = 4\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{4}<|im_end|>",
